---
/*
 * The bar above the onboarding column.
 *
 * /start renders Base with `bareHeader` AND `bareFooter`, so neither the site's sticky nav nor
 * its footer is on this page. That is deliberate: both carry several ways out, and a signup
 * flow that keeps offering them is a flow people leave. What stays is the one thing someone
 * needs mid-signup — a way back to the site.
 *
 * THE MARK IS NO LONGER REDRAWN HERE. It used to be, with the brand colours written as raw
 * hex (#7c6cff / #9b8fff / #34d399) because the original lived inside Base.astro's template,
 * which that pass did not own. The three values matched --accent, --accent-bright and
 * --success exactly at the time, so nothing looked wrong — but the next edit to tokens.css
 * would have recoloured the logo on three pages and left this one behind. It comes from the
 * shared Wordmark component now, which also carries the type settings this file's copy
 * restated.
 *
 * THE PREDICTED EDIT HAS LANDED. The palette is going light-first, so those three hexes are
 * now stale as well as duplicated — had they stayed, /start would be the one page still
 * wearing the dark-mode logo. They are quoted above only as a record of what was deleted.
 * This file holds no colour of its own and should acquire none: everything visible here is
 * either the Wordmark component or layout, so it themes for free.
 */

import Wordmark from "../Wordmark.astro";
---

<div class="sh">
  <Wordmark href="/" />
</div>

<style>
  .sh {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-block-size: 3rem;
  }
</style>
